messages.text:
Archive representative:

We accept the batch-specific extension provision as proposed: day-10 delivery, access cutoff and deletion deadlines remain fixed unless both parties agree in writing before that deadline to a revised date for the affected batch. The backup exclusion applies throughout any extension.

We will incorporate the agreed terms into the schedule, including:
- named specialist bound to studio confidentiality terms;
- calibration sheet plus up to 30 approved masked crops, with no uncropped donor masters;
- archive review of each reference set within one business day, with specialist access only after written approval;
- backup exclusion applied before first scan to all donor files, temporary files, derivatives and correction work;
- deletion confirmation identifying systems covered and confirming the batch stayed out of backup;
- 24-hour incident notification with named contacts and monitored email/phone;
- equipment-only photograph requiring prior written approval of photograph, caption and intended use.

We will provide the specialist’s name and both parties’ incident contact details before signature.
